Subject: Keep an activation record for frameless functions that call, and merge it into backtraces

What this does
  - `JSAotFlRec` (prev, func, pc) is the record a compiled function with no frame leaves
    on `rt->aot_fl_top` while it runs. Records live on the C stack and link innermost-first.
  - A backtrace merges the records with the interpreter's frames by C-stack address, so an
    error created below a frameless function names it, with the line of the call in progress.
    The merge assumes one downward-growing C stack per runtime (a runtime is used on one
    thread at a time); a debug build asserts that every record is on the C stack.
  - The unit layout carries the offset of `aot_fl_top`.

Why we need it
  A frameless function that calls another compiled function (a recursive one, say) has no
  JSRegRun, so its frame was missing from the stack text of an error the callee throws.

